From: accel-virt
Subject: [PATCH] A geometry shader with stream output rasterizes the stream its creation names

Shaders converted through the dxbc-spirv IR kept rasterizedStream at 0 in their metadata whatever stream CreateGeometryShaderWithStreamOutput named, so the pipeline rasterized stream 0 while the shader kept the position of the named stream only: every vertex emitted to stream 0 was drawn at an undefined position with undefined attributes, a point at the centre of the target. The metadata now carries the rasterized stream, as the SPIR-V shader path does.
---
diff --git a/src/dxvk/dxvk_shader_ir.cpp b/src/dxvk/dxvk_shader_ir.cpp
--- a/src/dxvk/dxvk_shader_ir.cpp
+++ b/src/dxvk/dxvk_shader_ir.cpp
@@ -290,8 +290,10 @@ namespace dxvk {
 
       int32_t rasterizedStream = 0u;
 
-      if (m_stage == dxbc_spv::ir::ShaderStage::eGeometry)
+      if (m_stage == dxbc_spv::ir::ShaderStage::eGeometry) {
         rasterizedStream = m_info.rasterizedStream;
+        m_metadata.rasterizedStream = rasterizedStream;
+      }
 
       m_metadata.outputs = convertIoMap(dxbc_spv::ir::IoMap::forOutputs(m_builder, uint32_t(rasterizedStream)));
 
